A '''reconciliation council''' ({{lang-bl|consejo de reconciliación}}) is a court-like [[w:Restorative practices|restorative]] organization at the [[communes of Balisca|communal]] level in [[Balisca]]. It was forged out of the country's [[Baliscan Revolution|revolutionary fervor]] and the 1920 [[Declaration of Cooperation and Reconciliation]]. The aim of these councils is to ensure that the grievances of Balisca's historically marginalized communities are addressed and {{W|self-determination}} is universally respected. These councils have been instrumental in achieving the reversal of discriminatory socioeconomic and cultural policies, the restoration of [[Indigenous nations in Balisca|indigenous sovereignty]], [[LGBT rights in Balisca|expansion of LGBTQ rights]], and the decentralization of politics.

The stated purpose of these councils is to build a fair, democratic and inclusive society in Balisca. Through carefully selected engagements and interventions, the councils seek to shape communal, cantonal, and regional approaches to transitional justice and reconciliation in Balisca by drawing on community intelligence as well as macro-trend research and comparative analysis. These councils publish their research, make policy recommendations, and perform extensive reconciliation work on the ground.

